From 6cdea3f60d32dfcb4bc9eef21ef74e83ac2ba1eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 17:09:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-79197: Use after free in V8 (4/4)

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8167220:
[deoptimizer] Make DeoptimizeFunction code parameter non-optional

Remove the default value `= {}` from the `code` parameter of
`Deoptimizer::DeoptimizeFunction`. This prevents call sites from
accidentally omitting `frame->LookupCode()` when deoptimizing from
a stack frame, eliminating the footgun that caused OSR stack
frames to be missed when stepping in the debugger.

Update `Runtime_DeoptimizeFunction`, `Runtime_DeoptimizeNow`, and
`Runtime_DeoptimizeFunctionOSR` in `src/runtime/runtime-test.cc` to
explicitly pass `function->code(isolate)`.

TAG=agy
